.TH "NOTIFICATION.SHOW_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Notification.show_event \- Notification: show event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]show\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]Notification\f[R]
interface fires when a \f[CR]Notification\f[R] is displayed.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqshow\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onshow = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Using the Notifications API
